cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its evaluation protocol, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LedgerSentry: real-time card fraud detection with a reject-to-review option and leakage-safe temporal evaluation"
authors:
  - family-names: Jafari
    given-names: Sepehr
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Aeripsen/ledgersentry"
url: "https://aeripsen.github.io/ledgersentry/"
abstract: >-
  A gradient-boosted card-fraud classifier that abstains on uncertain
  transactions and routes them to human review instead of forcing a fraud or
  legit call. Evaluated on a strictly temporal holdout of the public ULB
  credit-card fraud dataset (56,961 held-out transactions, 75 frauds) with
  bootstrap confidence intervals, calibration, a byte-identical reproduction
  check, and a FastAPI service, Streamlit dashboard and container deployment.
keywords:
  - fraud detection
  - selective classification
  - reject option
  - temporal evaluation
  - imbalanced classification
  - gradient boosting
  - FastAPI
